#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
debugtrace-mcp: one MCP server (stdio) for every app launched with
`build-and-sign --mcp`, so each coding agent on the Mac needs a single entry:

    claude mcp add -s user apps -- ~/Projects/DebugTrace/Tools/debugtrace-mcp

Apps don't have fixed ports. Each `bas --mcp` launch records a session in
~/.local/state/debugtrace/sessions/<bundle id>@<device>.json: the app, the
device, the URL its server bound, and the pid of the `devicectl --console`
process streaming its log. That process exits when the app does, so a
session whose pid is gone is over. The tools below never change, whichever
apps are running, so an agent session that started before an app launched
still works:

    apps                          what is running
    help(app, endpoint?)          the app's self-describing API, with schemas
    call(app, endpoint, arguments?)  run one endpoint
    trace(app, note?)             capture a debug trace and save the zip here
    inject(app, files?, run?)     apply edited Swift source to the running app, no rebuild

Apps are found two ways: the session records above, and Bonjour. Every dev
build that build-and-sign signs starts its server on each launch and
advertises it as _debugtrace._tcp. The record names nothing: it carries a
random nonce and a tag over it under the build's token, so only the key ledger
(~/.local/state/debugtrace/keys) that holds the token can tell which app it is,
and the app's identity comes from that ledger record. So an app that is
already running can be attached to without a relaunch. Bonjour
reaches the local network only; over Tailscale, use `bas --mcp`.

`debugtrace-mcp discover` prints what is found, as JSON (tokens left out),
for other tools on this Mac such as the appstore page.

`app` may be omitted when only one is running. Each launch has its own bearer
token, which bas passes to the app and keeps in the session record (mode 600),
so no agent needs a header configured; ~/.config/debugtrace/token is only a
fallback for servers started some other way. Standard library only.
"""

